<DocPage title="Privacy - Loopress" kicker={`privacy · last updated ${LAST_UPDATED}`} heading="Privacy." lede="Loopress runs on your machine and your sites. Here is the little that reaches us, and how to turn it off.">
  <h2>The CLI</h2>
  <p>
    <code>lps</code> talks to your WordPress sites directly. Your files, credentials and site data
    never pass through Loopress servers.
  </p>
  <p>
    When the CLI crashes, it sends an error report to Sentry so we can fix it. Before it leaves your
    machine, the report is scrubbed: arguments and flag values are removed (only flag names are
    kept), site URLs are blanked, and server responses are dropped. Turn it off with
    <code>lps telemetry disable</code>, or for a single run with <code>LOOPRESS_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>The WordPress plugin</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Light</strong> sends nothing to Loopress.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Full</strong> can report its own errors to Sentry, only after an administrator says yes in
      the plugin's Settings tab. It also checks loopress.dev for new versions, like any plugin update
      check.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>This website</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Contact form</strong>: your name, email and message, used only to reply.</li>
    <li><strong>Newsletter</strong>: if you subscribe, your email is stored with Brevo. Every email has an unsubscribe link.</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics</strong>: Vercel Analytics, aggregated and without cookies.</li>
    <li><strong>Theme</strong>: one local storage entry remembers light or dark mode. No tracking or advertising cookies.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>The Loopress console</h2>
  <p>
    If you sign in to console.loopress.dev with Google, we store your email address and a Google
    account identifier, never your Google password. Running <code>lps login</code> connects a project
    to that account and syncs its metadata and WordPress credentials, encrypted at rest.
  </p>

  <h2>Who processes it</h2>
  <p>
    Sentry (error reports), Brevo (email), Vercel (hosting and analytics), Google (console sign-in)
    and GitHub (code and releases), each under its own privacy policy. We do not sell your data or
    share it for anyone's marketing.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You can ask to access, correct, export or delete your data at any time through the
    <a href="/proto/contact">contact page</a>. We keep it while your account is active or as long as
    needed to answer you.
  </p>

  <p class="aside">loopress is a developer tool, not aimed at children under 16.</p>
</DocPage>
